    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGEyMjY2YWZlY2JmYTg1NjcxYjgxMDNlZTQ2MGRiMmQ5Mzc2NmI5Mzk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T18:51:15Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T18:51:15Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion,app): the lathe axis fit sets off-centre features aside\n\nA keyway's or cross hole's normal lines miss the axis, and the plain\nleast-squares concurrency fit let their area drag the fitted origin: a\n72-segment D20 shaft exactly on G54 with a short keyway fitted 0.15 mm\noff and was refused with advice (move the work offset) that cannot help.\n\naxis::fit now reweighs the plain fit (multiaxis/axis_robust.rs): facets\nwhose normal lines meet the candidate axis within the concurrency\ntolerance are kept, the rest set aside, and the line and its direction\nrefinement refitted on the kept set until it settles; the refit must\nstill pass the full judgement on every facet. A part with nothing set\naside keeps its plain fit bit for bit (goldens unchanged); fewer than\nhalf the answering area kept keeps the plain fit, marked untrusted.\naxis::fit_report exposes the share and trust; the spindle law names the\nset-aside share and keeps the move-the-offset advice for the misplaced\ncase only.\n\nFixes #71\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
