        "date": "2026-11-07T19:03:36Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app,motion): name the features a trusted lathe axis fit set aside\n\nA trusted spindle-law pass with features set aside (keyways, flats,\nholes, eccentric sections) no longer generates in silence: the op's\npath carries a non-blocking note naming the share of the turned\n(non-end-face) surface that is not turned, above a 0.05 % floor so a\nplain revolve says nothing; one decimal, never \"0.0%\". The untrusted\nrefusal now says the reading is biased by off-centre features and\nmoving the work offset may not fix it. The 50 %-area / 8-facet refit\nguard is documented as a backstop behind judge's 90 % share.\n\nRefs #71\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
